@startuml acp-integration
!include theme.iuml
title Live ACP integration — reusable module and first debug consumer
autonumber
actor User
participant "React /debug/agent\nexisting chat item registry" as UI
participant "Python/uv application API\ncommands + snapshots + events" as API
database "SQLite history/events\nimmutable image storage" as DB
box "One local runtime per session; Docker replacement later" #EAF2F8
participant "Session supervisor\nprivate workspace + Codex state" as S
participant "Pinned Codex ACP adapter\nCodex App Server" as C
participant "Session-scoped sample MCP\nfetch / publish / camera request" as M
end box
User -> UI : create / select chat
UI -> API : create or open application session
API -> DB : retain session identity and runtime mapping
API -> S : ensure runtime; initialize or resume saved ACP session
S -> C : initialize; session/new or resume\nexplicit MCP configuration
C --> S : capabilities + ACP session ID
S -> API : ready
API --> UI : snapshot + event cursor
UI -> API : subscribe after cursor
User -> UI : attach image + send text
UI -> API : upload bytes; submit(clientMessageId, image IDs)
API -> DB : validate/store images; persist message and turn once
API -> S : dispatch one prompt for this session
S -> C : session/prompt(text + negotiated images / local paths)
C -> M : fetch_image / request_camera / publish_image
M -> API : scoped request; file bytes for publication
API -> DB : commit domain result and immutable asset
API --> M : versioned result with stable references
M --> C : structured result + text fallback
C --> S : text chunks / tool call patches / native image generation
S -> API : normalized activity with turn and generation
API -> DB : update stable records; append durable events
API --> UI : records + resource references
UI -> UI : existing renderer registry mounts image / camera / tool views
User -> UI : inspect / download / reattach image
C --> S : original prompt's terminal response
S -> API : complete turn; release prompt slot
note over UI, DB
  Snapshot/event replay restores browser state; it does not create a new ACP session.
  Agent JSON is typed command/result data, not authority to replace backend state.
  Native image generation writes a local file; MCP publication makes it an app asset.
end note
note over S, M
  Separate private runtime state for every chat. No shared writable Codex home.
  Permissions are answered explicitly; Stop cancels the turn and its pending requests.
  Uncertain turns are interrupted, never blindly resent. Saved files/history survive.
  Local process separation is not the final Docker security boundary.
end note
legend bottom
  M-ACP.md: module contract and integration gates. ACP-AGENT-STATE.md: state ownership.
  Runtime orchestration, application auth, CAD delegation, and public deployment follow separately.
endlegend
@enduml
